TIP:  Aside from the transitional (F) leading into the “ba-ba-by” the whole song repeats a  (C) (Am) (Em) (G) chord progression with two measures for each chord.  But keeping the rhythm can be a little tricky with Dolores’s occasional hesitations.  The strumming pattern begins with an upstroke:  U  U-D-U-D    U  U-D-U-D  . . .  so if you get off track just snap an upstroke at the next chord change and pick up the rhythm.


